{"tool_name":"quadfinder","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"quadfinder","home":"https://github.com/xiuchengquek/QuadFinder","summary":"QuadFinder is a tool for the identification and analysis of quadruplex forming nucleotide sequences.","addition_date":"2017-02-10T14:14:24Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T14:09:34.859663Z","tool_type":["Web application"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:quadfinder","credit":[{"name":"GitHub Issues","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"https://github.com/xiuchengquek/QuadFinder/issues"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["proteomics.bio.tools"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Quadruplex formation site detection","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0429"},{"term":"Repeat sequence analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0237"},{"term":"Representative sequence identification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2233"},{"term":"Sequence analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2403"}]}],"name":"QuadFinder","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"ELIXIR-EE","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/nar/gkl299","metadata":{"abstract":"G-quadruplex secondary structures, which play a structural role in repetitive DNA such as telomeres, may also play a functional role at other genomic locations as targetable regulatory elements which control gene expression. The recent interest in application of quadruplexes in biological systems prompted us to develop a tool for the identification and analysis of quadruplex-forming nucleotide sequences especially in the RNA. Here we present Quadfinder, an online server for prediction and bioinformatics of uni-molecular quadruplex-forming nucleotide sequences. The server is designed to be user-friendly and needs minimal intervention by the user, while providing flexibility of defining the variants of the motif. The server is freely available at URL http://miracle.igib.res.in/quadfinder/. \u00a9 The